's really great  because Tara were getting to approach  her as a young girl who doesn't know  who's like she doesn't know her destiny  which is very classic Supergirl but she  also doesn't know who she can be she  does know her powers she doesn't know  that she's part of this grand legacy  she's just this  girl kind of coming into this big world  fighting for what she believed in  okay so how did you guys draw  inspiration from the line of DC  collectibles that was the easiest from a  movie before it showed us they showed us  these beautiful designs and our instinct  just started going wild you know when we  first saw this stuff we were like oh wow  this is such a daunting task there's so  many elements here to play with and we  have so much respect for these  characters we absolutely have to use  something that's really special and then  we started looking at these designs and  we were like oh well what if we did this  and like look at those tattoos oh my god  clearly should got those at a prison  camp  oh my god yeah and I like all the  stories to started rolling out from  awesome all the fun of the fun of the  story of that we get to reinvest like  any character we want to hit and and do  so in a way that again like Superman and  Batman have never been around so what  did that mean for these characters what  I mean for a Batgirl what does that mean  for Harley Quinn right right so Harley  is actually one of my favorite  characters just in the regular DC use so  getting the chance to do this version of  her that's a little bit more while a lot  a bit more self actualized but most  importantly if the Harley Quinn that is  getting to evolve without being  dependent on the Joker's great she came  from herself first in her relationship  with the garden for relationship with  Lex Luthor and from that kind of growth  she's the one who's going to be  inspiring the Joker oh my gosh I love  that I really get to like approach her  for a really honest really true really  powerful and then we get to look at the  Joker from this very kind of very Harley  Quinn place where he's always trying to  prove himself to her rather than the  other way around and if she's the one  who sort of always like kind of shunkan  him off to the side and and everyone to  all realizing like oh maybe like this  guy but like also like you like that's  been really fun to do if I use actors  that's a great question I think we have  a really cool take on Catwoman that I  can almost not talk about without  getting too spoilery about it when we  get to her in Episode seven and eight  you're going to get a lot of really cool  information about what's going on with  her but I think our Catwoman has some  really cool hidden depths and I think  the one that will throw just a tease is  that she's not Selina Kyle what what it  means to be cat  in this world isn't necessarily  dependent on being Selina and how that  relationship plays out is I think going  to be a very interesting wonder one you  guys I cannot wait for this series it  sounds like it's going to be incredible  thank you so much for sitting down with  me Roger I have one more question and  that is when does this launch August  16th we're going to be bi-weekly until  October and then we're gonna start going  weekly so after that you'll get Gotham  City Garage like every week work starts  digital goes physical very nice to see  you done yeah we're greatly excited  thank you guys thank you hey that's a  preview of Gotham City Garage and here's  the full list of DC comics you can pick  up this week  [Music]  [Music]  that's the news for now but make sure  you update your poll list for this week  and check back with us for more news  straight from San Diego comic-con also  this year we're going to be holding the  first ever DC all access panel Thursday  at San Diego comic-con so if you're at  the con come by say hi and see a really  cool panel we'll see you tomorrow Super  Friends
 

